Built compress.py with a standard-library-only record-transform helper, structure.py, supporting both requested commands. The archive stores its templates and vocabulary, so decoding does not require corpus.txt. Verified byte-identical CLI round trips, including decoding in an isolated folder without the corpus. Compressed 313,972 bytes to 3,469 bytes: 98.8951% reduction, versus 35,399 bytes for default zlib. The registered correctness-gated assay produced the same score in three consecutive runs.